---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TableOfContents from '../../components/sections/TableOfContents.astro';

const toc = [
	{ id: 'the-8-point-verification-checklist', label: 'The 8-Point Verification Checklist' },
	{ id: 'red-flags-summary', label: 'Red Flags Summary' },
	{ id: 'how-to-request-a-verified-quote', label: 'How to Request a Verified Quote' },
	{ id: 'faq', label: 'Frequently Asked Questions' }
];

const faq = [
	{
		question: 'How do I verify that a valve manufacturer is genuine?',
		answer: 'Follow the checklist in this guide: obtain and verify certification copies (UL/FM/CE/ISO), ask for batch hydrostatic test reports, request a pre-shipment sample, and — where possible — arrange a video factory tour or on-site inspection. Genuine manufacturers welcome these requests; resellers and shell companies typically hesitate or stall.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What documents should I request before placing a valve order?',
		answer: 'Minimum set: business licence, applicable product certificates (UL/FM/CE/LPCB/ISO), batch hydrostatic and seat-leakage test reports, material certificates for critical components, and an inspection clause in the commercial contract. For export, also confirm the required country-of-origin and customs documentation.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What is a reasonable MOQ and lead time for fire protection valves?',
		answer: 'Standard MOQs are typically 20–50 units per model depending on the valve type and size; production lead times are commonly 15–30 days. Samples are usually available before the bulk order. Lead time beyond 45 days without explanation is a red flag worth questioning.'
	},
	{
		question: 'How can I check factory quality beyond the documents?',
		answer: 'Ask for a live video walk-through of the production and test bay, request photos of the actual batch (not stock photos), and consider a third-party inspection (SGS/BV/TUV style) at pre-shipment. A factory that hides its floor is a factory with something to hide.'
	}
];

const referencePages = [
	{ slug: 'resilient-seat-flanged-gate-valve-z41x', name: 'Z41X Gate Valve' },
	{ slug: 'overground-fire-hydrant-ss100', name: 'SS100 Fire Hydrant' },
	{ slug: 'wet-alarm-check-valve-zsfz-150', name: 'ZSFZ Wet Alarm Valve' }
];
---

<Layout
	title="B2B Valve Sourcing Checklist: How to Verify a Fire Equipment Manufacturer"
	description="B2B valve sourcing checklist: 8-point verification — certificates, test reports, samples, factory audits, payment terms and red flags for China sourcing."
	type="article"
	faq={faq}
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 mb-16">
		<nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 flex gap-2">
			<a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<span class="text-gray-600">Guides</span>
		</nav>

		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Procurement Guide</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">B2B Valve Sourcing Checklist: How to Verify a Fire Equipment Manufacturer</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">Fire protection equipment is life-safety hardware — a counterfeit or under-tested valve can fail in exactly the emergency it exists for. Yet the sector is full of trading companies presenting themselves as manufacturers. This checklist is the same 8-point diligence our own buyers run on us. Use it on every supplier, including us.</p>

			
			<TableOfContents headings={toc} />

			<h2 id="the-8-point-verification-checklist" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">The 8-Point Verification Checklist</h2>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">1. Certificates — verify, don't collect</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Ask for the actual certificate documents (UL, FM, CE, LPCB, ISO 9001) and check three things: the certificate holder name matches the manufacturer, the standard/edition is current, and the product range on the certificate covers the exact model you are buying. Logos in a brochure prove nothing. A genuine manufacturer will publish its certification package — ours is on the <a href="/certificates/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">certificates page</a>.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">2. Test reports — batch, not template</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">A generic test certificate can be downloaded from anywhere. Request the hydrostatic and seat-leakage test reports for the <em>actual batch</em> you will receive, with serial numbers and dates. If the supplier cannot produce batch-level reports, your "manufacturer" may not have a test bay at all.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">3. Factory evidence — video or visit</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">A live video walk-through of the production line and hydraulic test bench takes ten minutes and eliminates most imposters. If a supplier refuses or insists on stock photos, treat it as a red flag. For large orders, budget for a third-party inspection (SGS/BV-style) at pre-shipment.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">4. Sample before bulk</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Order one sample unit first. Test it against your spec, weigh it, and compare the casting quality and coating thickness to the factory photos. Samples are cheap insurance — and a genuine factory will happily sell you one.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">5. Company substance</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Check the business licence, factory address and how long the company has been operating. Look for a real website with technical depth (specs, datasheets, guides), not a one-page storefront. A manufacturer that has shipped for years leaves a traceable trail of technical content.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">6. Payment terms</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">For first orders, a 30/70 split (30% deposit, 70% against B/L or inspection) is standard practice. Be wary of demands for full payment upfront or payments to personal accounts. Use a letter of credit or a secured payment method until trust is established.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">7. Lead time and communication</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">A competent factory answers technical questions in writing within one working day and commits to a production schedule it can keep. Vague lead times, evasive answers on test data, or salespeople who cannot explain their own product's specs are warning signs.</p>

			<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">8. Spares and support</h3>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Ask about spare parts (seals, stems, couplings) and after-sales support before you order, not after commissioning. A manufacturer that stocks spares and documents maintenance procedures is building a long-term relationship; a trader disappears after the shipment.</p>

			<h2 id="red-flags-summary" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">Red Flags Summary</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li>Cannot produce batch-level test reports</li>
				<li>Certificate holder name does not match the "factory" name</li>
				<li>Refuses video tour or live inspection</li>
				<li>Requires 100% payment upfront</li>
				<li>Sales team cannot answer basic specification questions</li>
				<li>Only stock photos, no technical documentation, no engineering depth on the website</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="how-to-request-a-verified-quote" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">How to Request a Verified Quote</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">A good inquiry gets a good response. Include: product type and model, DN/PN, connection standard, required certification (UL/FM/CE/other), target quantity, destination country and port. A supplier that answers with a structured datasheet and test plan — not just a price — is demonstrating exactly the competence the checklist above verifies.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Browse representative certified products to see the documentation standard we ship with: the <a href="/products/resilient-seat-flanged-gate-valve-z41x/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Z41X gate valve</a>, <a href="/products/overground-fire-hydrant-ss100/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">SS100 fire hydrant</a> and <a href="/products/wet-alarm-check-valve-zsfz-150/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZSFZ wet alarm valve</a>. Then run this checklist on us — we publish our <a href="/certificates/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">certificates</a>, our <a href="/about/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">company profile</a>, and we answer technical questions in writing within one working day.</p>

			<!-- Related guide -->
			<div class="mt-10 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Related Guide: UL Valve Selection</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Choosing the right UL listed valve type and verifying genuine certificates? Read <a href="/guides/how-to-choose-ul-listed-fire-valves/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">How to Choose UL Listed Fire Valves</a>.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQ Section -->
			<h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4">
				{faq.map(item => (
					<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30">
						<summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer list-none">
							<span>{item.question}</span>
							<span class="text-brand-blue text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">{item.answer}</p>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>

			<!-- CTA -->
			<div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
				<div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue to-blue-800 px-6 sm:px-10 py-10 text-center">
					<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Ready to Test Us Against This Checklist?</h2>
					<p class="mt-3 text-blue-100 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm leading-relaxed">Send your RFQ — we reply with certifications, batch test reports and a datasheet, not just a price.</p>
					<div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
						<a href="/contact/" class="px-8 py-4 bg-brand-red text-white font-bold rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition">Send Your RFQ</a>
						<a href="https://wa.me/8618684324501?text=Hi%2C%20I%27d%20like%20to%20verify%20your%20factory%20and%20send%20an%20RFQ" class="px-8 py-4 bg-white text-brand-blue font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
